  <wpt lat="45.865761" lon="-84.630531">
    <name>Mackinac Island</name>
    <desc>Mackinac Island has no cars and is reached only by ferry. The legacy page drew it as a separate bonus marker (calcRoute('Mackinac Island, MI', 'Mackinac Island, MI', [])) with no leg, after the main loop had already closed at Ypsilanti. Verified 2026-09-26: matches Wikidata coordinate for the island within ~50m (wikidata:Q1431148). drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Shepler's Mackinac Island ferry dock in Mackinaw City (osm:node/2321023823, wikidata:Q7494519). Order fixed 2026-09-26: moved from the end of the list (where the loop ran Ann Arbor -&gt; island -&gt; Ypsilanti, adding about 500 mi that the 2015 route never drove) to between Mackinaw City and St Ignace, the ferry crossing the island lies on; the stop now adds about 1 mi and the loop closes Ann Arbor -&gt; Ypsilanti as in 2015</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.868668" lon="-84.727815">
    <name>St Ignace</name>
    <desc>St Ignace</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.497673" lon="-84.347658">
    <name>Sault Ste. Marie</name>
    <desc>Sault Ste. Marie</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.548253" lon="-86.344739">
    <name>Pictured Rocks National Lakeshore</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within ~3km of the Wikidata park point (wikidata:Q3382575); query specifies the Grand Marais (east) end of this large park; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Grand Sable Visitor Center on H-58 at the Grand Marais end named in the query (osm:way/233579437)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.543611" lon="-87.395556">
    <name>Marquette</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; display and drive point fixed 2026-09-26: moved 20.5 km to the Wikidata point for the city of Marquette (wikidata:Q12443); the old Nominatim point (46.4481521,-87.6305899) was in the county interior near Ishpeming, not the city</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.391577" lon="-88.013163">
    <name>Mt Bohemia</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Wikidata coordinate within ~40m; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Mount Bohemia base-area parking by the lodge and bus pickup (osm:way/936922785)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.119689" lon="-88.562547">
    <name>Keweenaw Peninsula</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within the Keweenaw Peninsula near Schoolcraft Township as named in the query; the peninsula's own Wikidata centroid (wikidata:Q12430) is ~12.6km further north, both plausible for this large peninsula with no address given</desc>
  </wpt>
